        content: "On the Text Replacement screen, look at the top-right corner for a plus sign (+). Tap it. A new screen opens with two fields. The top field is labeled \"Phrase\" and the bottom field is labeled \"Shortcut.\" The Phrase is the full text you want your iPhone to type out. The Shortcut is the short code you will type. Type your full home address into the Phrase field, including the street, city, state, and zip code on one line. Then tap the Shortcut field and type \"myadr\" or \"homeadr\" or whatever short code you want.",
        warning: "Do not pick a shortcut that is also a real word. If you pick \"home\" as the shortcut, every time you type the word home in any text, your iPhone will replace it with your full address."
